<span id="A4.T12.2.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:199.2pt;">
<span id="A4.T12.2.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">The fastest individual is NAME_3. Step-by-Step Explanation: 1. Given Information: NAME_1 is faster than NAME_2: NAME_1 <math id="A4.T12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> NAME_2. NAME_1 is slower than NAME_3: NAME_3 <math id="A4.T12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> NAME_1. 2. Combine the Inequalities: From the two points, we can chain the inequalities: NAME_3 <math id="A4.T12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> NAME_1 <math id="A4.T12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&gt;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>&gt;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&gt;</annotation></semantics></math> NAME_2. 3. Determine the Fastest: The highest in the chain is NAME_3, making them the fastest. Answer: The fastest individual is NAME_3.</span>
</span></td></tr>
